          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong weak limit
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            over that diagram which satisfies the existence property of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            but not necessarily the uniqueness. The dual concept is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+colimit"} weak colimit
          %p
            Beware that “weak” here does
            %strong not
            correspond to that in “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+n-category"}> weak n-category
            ”, in particular it does
            %strong not
            refer to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToHomotopyLimits"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            play a key role in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
          %h2#weak_pullbacks Weak pullbacks
          %p
            A
            %strong weak pullback
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi g
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A\overset{f}{\to} C \overset{g}{\leftarrow} B
          %p
            (in some
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagram"} commutative square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P &amp; \overset{p}{\to} &amp; A
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{q}} \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                  \\\
                  B &amp; \overset{g}{\to} &amp; C
                  }
          %p such that for every commuting square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ X &amp; \overset{x}{\to} &amp; A\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{y}} \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}\\
                  B &amp; \overset{g}{\to} &amp; C}
          %p
            there exists a morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \colon X\to P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi h
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = h p
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = h q
          %p
            If the actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \underset{C}{\times}B
            exists, then this condition means equivalently that the universal morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P \longrightarrow A \underset{C}{\times}B
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} split epimorphism
          %h2#weak_terminal_objects Weak terminal objects
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
            is a weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            from any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            to any inhabited set. But only a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            is a terminal object.
          %h2#projective_objects_and_exact_completion Projective objects and exact completion
          %p
            In any category with finite limits and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} enough projectives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi g
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\overset{f}{\to} C \overset{g}{\leftarrow} B
            of projective objects, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to A\times_C B
            be a projective cover of the actual pullback; then any square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ X &amp; \overset{x}{\to} &amp; A\\
                  ^y \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow ^f\\
                  B &amp; \overset{g}{\to} &amp; C}
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            projective induces a morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi C
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to A\times_C B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to P
            since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is projective.
          %p
            Conversely, from any category with weak finite limits one can construct an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+category"} exact completion
            in which the original category sits as the projective objects, and the exact categories constructible in this way are precisely those having enough projectives.
          %h2#RelationToHomotopyLimits Relation to homotopy limits
          %p
            Unlike usages of ‘weak’ in terms like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+n-category"} weak n-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopies
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} equivalences
          %p
            However, some homotopy limits induce the corresponding type of weak limit in the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ P &amp; \overset{p}{\to} &amp; A\\
                  ^q \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow ^f\\
                  B &amp; \overset{g}{\to} &amp; C}
          %p
            is a homotopy pullback in some category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            having a notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(M)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ X &amp; \overset{x}{\to} &amp; A\\
                  ^y \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow ^f\\
                  B &amp; \overset{g}{\to} &amp; C}
          %p
            that commutes in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(M)
            commutes up to homotopy in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to P
            and homotopies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi h
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p h \simeq x
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mi h
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q h\simeq y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(M)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            is unique up to homotopy, this is only true for a given
            %em choice
            of homotopy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi g
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f x \simeq g y
            = succeed "\u2018s." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(M)
            %em existence
            of homotopies, we have only a weak pullback.
          %p
            Note, though, that not
            %em all
            homotopy limits produce weak limits in the homotopy category, because in general it will not be possible to lift a cone that commutes in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(M)
            to a cone that commutes up to
            %em coherent
            homotopy in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            give actual (not weak) products in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(M)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+adjoint"} weak adjoint
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+multilimit"} weak multilimit
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
              ,
              %em Representations in abelian categories
              1966 Proc. Conf. Categorical Algebra (La Jolla, Calif., 1965) pp. 95–120 Springer, New York
        .revisedby
